        "statement": {
          "before": "Assume full AC. Every nonempty smooth oriented link $L\\subset S^3$ bounds a connected compact smooth oriented embedded surface. If $F$ is any such surface with Seifert matrix $V$, and $u$ is a formal Laurent variable, then\n$$D_L(u)=\\det(u^{-1}V-uV^T)$$\nis independent of the surface and integral basis, belongs to $\\mathbb Z[u-u^{-1}]$, equals $1$ for the unknot, and satisfies\n$$D_{L_+}(u)-D_{L_-}(u)=(u-u^{-1})D_{L_0}(u)$$\nfor every oriented skein triple. Thus $D_L(u)=\\nabla_L(u-u^{-1})$ for the unique Conway polynomial normalized by $\\nabla_U=1$ and $\\nabla_+-\\nabla_-=z\\nabla_0$.",
          "after": "Assume full AC. Every nonempty smooth oriented link $L\\subset S^3$ bounds a connected compact smooth oriented embedded surface. If $F$ is any such surface with Seifert matrix $V$, and $u$ is a formal Laurent variable, define the Seifert determinant\n$$\\Theta_L(u):=\\det(u^{-1}V-uV^T).$$\nIt is independent of the surface and integral basis, belongs to $\\mathbb Z[u-u^{-1}]$, equals $1$ for the unknot, and satisfies\n$$\\Theta_{L_+}(u)-\\Theta_{L_-}(u)=(u-u^{-1})\\Theta_{L_0}(u)$$\nfor every oriented skein triple. Thus $\\Theta_L(u)=\\nabla_L(u-u^{-1})$ for the unique Conway polynomial normalized by $\\nabla_U=1$ and $\\nabla_+-\\nabla_-=z\\nabla_0$."
        }
